<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's JSE details amendments to some indices.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's JSE details amendments to some indices.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Johannesburg Stock Exchange on Tuesday detailed a number of amendments to some of its key indices following a bi-annual revision.</p>
<p>It said the changes will be effective from the close of business on June 20.</p>
<p>The JSE said that new inclusions in the ALSI40 index (JSE Overall 40) were Tiger Oats, Persetel NBS and Southern Life. Exclusions from this index are Kloof, Amcoal, M&amp;R Hold and Freegold.</p>
<p>The FINDI30 index (the financial top 30) will from Friday include Didata, Southern Life, Metlife and Persetel, while it will exclude Naspers &quot;N&quot; shares, M&amp;R Hold, Charter and Premier Group.</p>
<p>The INDI25 index (JSE Industrial 25) will take on Didata, Persetel and Plate Glass, while it will lose Pepkor, Engen and the Premier Group.</p>
<p>The GOLD10 index (JSE All Gold 10) will include Avgold but exclude Randfontein.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
